  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile + avgpool is much better than singleprofile or transformer aggregation for both RNA and image models, with RNA-only PCA multiprofile avgpool reaching 0.5907 accuracy. The key remaining uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion can improve over the strong RNA-only baseline when the same profile, aggregation, and tested encoders are held fixed. config_018 keeps PCA, ResNet50, multiprofile, and avgpool constant and only adds concat fusion, allowing a direct comparison against config_002 and config_011. This is the cleanest next test of whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing before spending budget on stronger encoders or more complex fusion variants."
